WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.420
Last quarter, two of our client decks went out
with numbers an AI tool made up.

2
00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:09.580
One client caught it, in the meeting,
in front of the partner.

3
00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:16.970
This module isn't about avoiding AI.
Used well, it saves you hours every week.

4
00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:21.170
The trouble is what slips through
when nobody checks.

5
00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:27.840
AI tools make three kinds of mistakes.
They invent facts, and even sources.

6
00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:32.330
They carry bias.
And their summaries leave things out.

7
00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:35.590
They sound just as confident either way.

8
00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:41.240
The fourth risk is on us:
putting client data where it shouldn't go.

9
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:45.500
Only approved tools,
and only the data the task needs.

10
00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:51.950
In this course, you'll spend a Friday afternoon
as Maya, an analyst three months in,

11
00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:55.750
with a deck due at six.
You'll make three calls.

12
00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:00.110
Every choice costs time,
and you'll see how Monday goes.

13
00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.730
When you're done, keep the one-page checklist.

14
00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:07.650
Four checks, a few minutes each.
Let's get started.
